ow to Join a Windows 11 Device to Microsoft Entra ID
🔹 Requirements:

Windows 11 Pro, Enterprise, or Education (Home edition does not support Entra ID Join)

A Microsoft 365 Business or Enterprise subscription

A licensed user account in Microsoft Entra ID (Azure AD)

Internet connection

Option 1: Join During Initial Setup (Out-of-box experience)
If you're setting up a new device or resetting Windows 11:

Power on the device and begin the Windows 11 setup process.

Choose your region and keyboard layout, then proceed.

On the "Let’s add your Microsoft account" or "Sign in with Microsoft" screen, enter the Entra ID (Microsoft 365) email and password.

If prompted, complete Multi-Factor Authentication (MFA).

Windows will automatically join the device to Entra ID, apply any Intune/Endpoint Manager policies, and prepare the desktop.

Option 2: Join an Existing Windows 11 Device to Entra ID
If the device is already running Windows 11:

Open Settings
→ Start > Settings > Accounts

Go to Access work or school
→ Click “Access work or school” in the left menu.

Click “Connect”

In the dialog box, choose:
→ “Join this device to Entra ID” (You may see it as "Join this device to Azure Active Directory" on older builds)

Enter the user’s Microsoft 365 (Entra ID) email address, then click Next.

Enter the user’s password and complete MFA, if required.

Review the account and organization details, then click Join.

After the device is successfully joined, click Done.

Restart the computer.

On the login screen, choose Other user, and sign in with the Entra ID credentials (e.g. user@company.com).

Optional: Verify the Join Status
To confirm the device is joined:

Go to Settings > System > About

Scroll to "Device specifications" > "Domain or workgroup"

It should say: Azure AD joined

Or open Command Prompt and run:

dsregcmd /status
Look under "AzureAdJoined" = YES

